.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SSL_SET1_INITIAL_PEER_ADDR 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SSL_set1_initial_peer_addr
.Nd set the initial peer address for a QUIC connection
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ssl.h
.Ft int
.Fo SSL_set1_initial_peer_addr
.Fa "SSL *s"
.Fa "const BIO_ADDR *addr"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn SSL_set1_initial_peer_addr
sets the initial destination peer address to be used for the purposes of
establishing a QUIC connection in client mode.
This function can be used only on a QUIC connection SSL object, and can
be used only before a connection attempt is first made.
.Fa addr
must point to a
.Sy BIO_ADDR
representing a UDP destination address of the server to connect to.
.Pp
Where a QUIC connection object is provided with a write BIO which
supports the
.Sy BIO_CTRL_DGRAM_GET_PEER
control (for example,
.Sy BIO_s_dgram Ns ),
the initial destination peer address can be detected automatically; if
.Sy BIO_CTRL_DGRAM_GET_PEER
returns a valid
.Pf (non- Sy AF_UNSPEC )
peer address and no valid peer address has yet been set, this will be
set automatically as the initial peer address.
This behaviour can be overridden by calling
.Fn SSL_set1_initial_peer_addr
with a valid peer address explicitly.
.Pp
The destination address used by QUIC may change over time in response to
connection events, such as connection migration (where supported).
.Fn SSL_set1_initial_peer_addr
configures the destination address used for initial connection
establishment, and does not confer any guarantee about the destination
address being used for communication at any later time in the connection
lifecycle.
.Pp
This function makes a copy of the address passed by the caller; the
.Sy BIO_ADDR
structure pointed to by
.Fa addr
may be freed by the caller after this function returns.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Returns 1 on success and 0 on failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr BIO_ADDR 3 ,
.Xr ssl 7
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn SSL_set1_initial_peer_addr
function was added in OpenSSL 3.2.
